:: Day3_Afternoon_A_Return [day3 afternoon chloe park purse return]
<<nobr>>
<p>"Here." I hold the purse back out to her. "I'll carry the picnic stuff instead."</p>

<p>A flicker crosses her face. Fast. Controlled. She takes the purse back and slings it over her shoulder.</p>

<<dialog "Chloe" "You're so worried about what people think.">>

<p>It's not angry. It's not even disappointed. It's observational. Like she's noting a data point. A test result. The hypothesis was that I'd carry it. The result is that I didn't. She adjusts her model and moves on.</p>

<p>The rest of the afternoon is fine. Normal. But there's a thin frost on everything, an invisible layer between us that wasn't there before. She doesn't rest her head on my shoulder on the walk back.</p>

<p>We pass Mrs. Delgado's bench on the way out. She watches me pass with the same milky-sharp eyes as always. "Still that boy from the Chambers house," she murmurs. Not to me. To the pigeons. "Getting thinner. Or taller. Or something."</p>

<<statChange "resistance" 3>>
<<set $chloeRelationship -= 1>>
